@startuml PendingConsent

title Inquiry Pending Consent API Sequence

' Visual style
skinparam defaultFontName "Sarabun"
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 10
skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #475569
    ArrowFontColor #334155
    LifeLineBorderColor #CBD5E1
    LifeLineBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
    ParticipantBorderColor #94A3B8
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #F1F5F9
    ParticipantFontColor #0F172A
    GroupBorderColor #94A3B8
    GroupBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
    GroupFontColor #334155
}

' Do not show participant footers at the bottom of the diagram
hide footbox
actor "User" as user
box "Frontend" #F8FAFC
    participant "Consent Page" as page
end box
box "Web API" #F8FAFC
    participant "API" as api
    participant "Application" as app
    participant "Domain" as domain
    participant "Infrastructure" as infra
end box
box "Database" #F8FAFC
    database "t_user_access_token" as t_user_access_token
    database "t_consent" as t_consent
    database "t_user_consent" as t_user_consent
    database "m_consent_type" as m_consent_type
end box
user -> page: Request pending consents
activate page
page -> api: GET v1/consent/pending (Bearer JWT, timestamp, requestId)
activate api
api -> app: [**InquiryPendingConsentQueryHandler**] Process request
activate app
app -> app: Create requestId if omitted; validate mandatory UTC timestamp
note over app, infra
    Validate the mandatory timestamp as a UTC timestamp before SQL; invalid/missing timestamp returns 400
    E10001. Generate requestId when omitted. Missing/malformed/invalid Bearer credentials return the same 401
    E10002 `Invalid or expired access token.` Verify JWT signature, issuer, audience, exp and UUID sub; derive
    userId only from verified sub and accessTokenHash as SHA-256 (32 bytes) of the exact JWT. This endpoint
    requires no administrator role or assignment-table query and only returns that user's pending state.
end note
alt Missing or invalid timestamp
    app -> api: HTTP 400 E10001
    api -> page: Header validation error
else Valid ordinary headers
    app -> app: Verify JWT signature/issuer/audience/exp/UUID sub
    alt Missing, malformed or invalid JWT
        app -> api: HTTP 401 E10002 Invalid or expired access token.
        api -> page: Authentication error
    else Verified JWT
        app -> app: userId = verified sub; accessTokenHash = SHA-256 exact JWT
        app -> infra: BEGIN ISOLATION LEVEL REPEATABLE READ READ ONLY
        note over app, infra
            Capture UTC now immediately before the first credential query, which establishes the transaction snapshot.
            Check the stored access token hash, verified userId, ACTIVE token, unexpired stored expiry and ACTIVE user
            together; recheck JWT expiry at now. Failure rolls back and returns 401 before consent queries. Every later
            policy/evidence/type query uses this same snapshot and now, so a type name, version or submission cannot
            change halfway through the response. No FOR UPDATE, advisory lock or evidence write is needed for this
            inquiry.
            Finish the read-only transaction with COMMIT before 200. On timeout before commit, ROLLBACK then 408 E90001;
            on unexpected pre-commit failure (including incomplete response mapping), ROLLBACK then generic 500 with no
            new bizCode. No pending/credential/error path inserts, updates or deletes data; no response includes stored
            token hashes or internal evidence ids.
        end note
        alt Read-only work completes
            app -> app: Capture UTC now before first query; establish snapshot and recheck JWT exp
            app -> infra: QUERY - Check active credential and user
            infra -> t_user_access_token: QUERY - Check active credential and user
            activate t_user_access_token
                note right of t_user_access_token
                    SELECT
                        at.user_id
                    FROM authen.t_user_access_token at
                    WHERE at.token = '<sequence.accessTokenHash>'
                    AND at.user_id = '<sequence.userId>'
                    AND at.row_status = 'ACTIVE'
                    AND at.expired_at > '<sequence.now>'
                    AND EXISTS (
                        SELECT 1
                        FROM authen.m_user u
                        WHERE u.id = at.user_id
                        AND u.row_status = 'ACTIVE'
                    )
                end note
                t_user_access_token -> infra: Return ACTIVE matching token/user or no row
            deactivate t_user_access_token
            infra -> app: Return ACTIVE matching token/user or no row
            alt Credential/user ACTIVE and stored/JWT expiry valid at now
                app -> infra: QUERY - Get pending consents
                infra -> t_consent: QUERY - Get pending consents
                activate t_consent
                    note right of t_consent
                        SELECT
                            c.id as consent_id,
                            c.code,
                            c.consent_type_id,
                            c.consent_version,
                            c.consent_name,
                            c.consent_description,
                            c.effective_at,
                            c.expired_at,
                            c.is_required,
                            c.body
                        FROM consent.t_consent c
                        WHERE c.row_status = 'ACTIVE'
                        AND c.effective_at <= '<sequence.now>'
                        AND (c.expired_at IS NULL OR c.expired_at > '<sequence.now>')
                        AND EXISTS (
                            SELECT 1
                            FROM consent.m_consent_type ct
                            WHERE ct.id = c.consent_type_id
                            AND ct.row_status = 'ACTIVE'
                        )
                        AND NOT COALESCE((
                            SELECT uc.is_read AND (NOT c.is_required OR uc.result)
                            FROM authen.t_user_consent uc
                            WHERE uc.user_id = '<sequence.userId>'
                            AND uc.consent_id = c.id
                            AND uc.consent_version = c.consent_version
                            AND uc.row_status = 'ACTIVE'
                            ORDER BY uc.created_at DESC, uc.id DESC
                            LIMIT 1
                        ), FALSE)
                        ORDER BY c.effective_at, c.id
                    end note
                    t_consent -> infra: Return ordered pendingConsents (all current fields, type ids)
                deactivate t_consent
                infra -> app: Return ordered pendingConsents (all current fields, type ids)
                alt pendingConsents is empty
                    app -> app: data.consents = []; skip history/type lookups
                else pendingConsents is non-empty
                    app -> app: consentIds = pendingConsents.consent_id; consentTypeIds = distinct pending type ids
                    app -> infra: QUERY - Get latest submitted version
                    infra -> t_user_consent: QUERY - Get latest submitted version
                    activate t_user_consent
                        note right of t_user_consent
                            SELECT DISTINCT ON (uc.consent_id)
                                uc.consent_id,
                                uc.consent_version as submitted_version
                            FROM authen.t_user_consent uc
                            WHERE uc.user_id = '<sequence.userId>'
                            AND uc.consent_id = ANY ('<sequence.consentIds>'::UUID[])
                            AND uc.row_status = 'ACTIVE'
                            ORDER BY uc.consent_id, uc.created_at DESC, uc.id DESC
                        end note
                        t_user_consent -> infra: Return latest ACTIVE submittedVersion by consentId
                    deactivate t_user_consent
                    infra -> app: Return latest ACTIVE submittedVersion by consentId
                    app -> infra: QUERY - Get consent type
                    infra -> m_consent_type: QUERY - Get consent type
                    activate m_consent_type
                        note right of m_consent_type
                            SELECT
                                ct.id as consent_type_id,
                                ct.name as consent_type_name
                            FROM consent.m_consent_type ct
                            WHERE ct.id = ANY ('<sequence.consentTypeIds>'::UUID[])
                            AND ct.row_status = 'ACTIVE'
                            ORDER BY ct.id
                        end note
                        m_consent_type -> infra: Return ACTIVE type names by typeId
                    deactivate m_consent_type
                    infra -> app: Return ACTIVE type names by typeId
                    app -> domain: Merge twelve response fields; submittedVersion = latest map or null; require every type name
                    domain -> app: Return complete data.consents in effective_at ASC, id ASC order
                    app -> app: Mapping failure throws before COMMIT; use unexpected-failure path
                end
                app -> infra: COMMIT
                infra -> app: Return completed read-only transaction
                note over app, infra
                    This detailed endpoint revision remains in-review; it includes no backend implementation.
                    A request whose credential/user was revoked before that snapshot is rejected; an already-authorized
                    in-flight read may finish against its established snapshot. This does not revive a revoked token or
                    authorize a later request. This read-only snapshot must not be reused by submission, which takes the user
                    lock and rechecks fresh token state as specified in its own API review.
                    A consent with an inactive/locked/archived/deleted type is hidden even if the consent itself is ACTIVE.
                    Required means c.is_required, not a type default.
                    Only that row determines pending; do not let any older accepted duplicate hide a newer rejection or unread
                    row. Evidence for another user, another version or a non-ACTIVE row never clears pending. The same canonical
                    rule is specified by submit-consent's separate review; older/history rows are retained.
                    Required consent is complete only when the canonical current-version row has BOTH is_read=true AND
                    result=true. Missing evidence, unread acceptance, read-only/default false and explicit rejection all remain
                    pending. Optional consent is complete once canonical current-version is_read=true, regardless of result. An
                    unread optional acceptance still remains pending. No evidence means pending for either kind. A new current
                    version is pending even if an older version was accepted.
                    For the non-empty pending list, collect pending consentIds and distinct consentTypeIds, then load latest
                    ACTIVE recorded version across all versions and the type names. Both queries use typed UUID arrays and the
                    same snapshot. Latest recorded version means newest created_at, then greatest id, including a read-only
                    record; submittedVersion does not itself prove acceptance and may equal the current version while a required
                    consent is still pending. Map no evidence to explicit null, never a default version or empty string.
                    Keep pending results ordered by effective_at ASC, id ASC. Map each row to consentId, code, consentTypeId,
                    consentTypeName, consentVersion, submittedVersion, consentName, consentDescription, effectiveAt, expiredAt,
                    isRequired and body; preserve this order after merging query results. Type names are mandatory: the same
                    snapshot's ACTIVE-type predicate and lookup guarantee the referenced name. A missing type-name mapping is an
                    internal consistency failure, not a partly populated success. Do not silently expose hidden types to fill
                    that name.
                    If no pending rows exist, skip history/type lookups and return 200 S10000 with data.consents=[] after
                    COMMIT. There is no 404 for an empty list. The SQL's NOT COALESCE handles missing evidence as pending; never
                    treat NULL as acceptance. Parameters are typed bound values, not interpolated strings.
                    This GET never marks a consent read, changes result/read_at or writes any history. The frontend calls
                    submit-consent with the displayed version and isRead=true when it actually displays that consent; it adds
                    result later on that same endpoint (Q16/Q17). Merely fetching this list creates no read evidence. Required
                    pending does not block login or other APIs (Q9).
                    Pending truth table for a visible current consent: | Canonical evidence | Required | Optional | |
                    ---------------------------------------------- | -------- | -------- | | None, other version/user, or
                    non-ACTIVE only | Pending | Pending | | isRead=false, result=false | Pending | Pending | | isRead=false,
                    result=true | Pending | Pending | | isRead=true, result=false (read-only/rejected) | Pending | Complete | |
                    isRead=true, result=true | Complete | Complete |
                end note
                app -> api: HTTP 200 S10000 Inquiry Pending Consent Success; data.consents
                api -> page: Return ordered list or [] without recording reading
                page -> user: Display pending items; call submit separately when displaying content
            else Credential/user inactive, revoked or expired
                app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                app -> api: HTTP 401 E10002 Invalid or expired access token.
                api -> page: Authentication error
            end
        else Timeout before COMMIT
            app -> infra: ROLLBACK
            app -> api: HTTP 408 E90001
            api -> page: Inquiry timed out
        else Unexpected pre-commit failure including incomplete mapping
            app -> infra: ROLLBACK
            app -> api: HTTP 500 Internal Server Error; omit bizCode
            api -> page: Generic inquiry failure
        end
    end
end
deactivate app
deactivate api
deactivate page
@enduml
